  "standard_prerequisites": [],
  "core_obligations": [
    "The author constructs the determinant-transgression 2-form on the quotient by reparametrisations and fibre rotation, identifies its kernel, and then computes arbitrary curvature-functional variations while controlling the noncommuting arclength/time derivatives. This produces the shifted adjoint recursion operator R*+4 and explicit Hamiltonian density combinations; subtracting the 4-shift gives the full geometric mKdV hierarchy. Vizman closed-form calculus and Olver bi-Hamiltonian recursion are actual priors, but neither supplies this quotient/variation/curvature-lift construction. Individual differentiation formulas and the final telescoping identity alone are H1 and not extra units."
  ],
  "proof_roadmap": [
    "Full original article and all original figures/references preserved. Counted primary is the symplectic Hamiltonian realization with its full variation chain. Stationary-curve quadratures remain a complete worked application at original author granularity; experimental observations starting1231 and prospective directions1376-1388 are explicitly unproved and not included in the counted claim."
  ],
